# Sarros coding standards

- Follow existing project patterns first.
- Keep business logic out of UI components when the repo already has service/helper layers.
- Validate API inputs and external payloads at boundaries.
- Do not invent schemas, environment variables, API routes, or integration contracts.
- Avoid adding dependencies unless clearly justified.
- Protect secrets and customer data.
- Use clear names and simple control flow.
- Keep changes narrow and reviewable.
